From 88b27053114706904ae02cd3399cb768a1f5179c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:15:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] r4 journey fix 3: prewarm the journey water shader/PSO
 under the set-off black (no first-sight hitch)

WebGL links the water program and Cocos builds the PSO on the first draw, which
was whenever the lake first entered the walking camera's view. On the first
show(true) (under the set-off fade's full black, right after prime() switched
the fog, so the compiled variant is the one the lake uses), the journey now
draws its own water copy once on a copy of the real lake mesh, shrunk to <=1 mm
in front of the journey camera, for 2 rendered frames (3 s cap if no draw
event), then removes it. Same mesh/material/shadow flags/layer as the lake.
Once per journey, cancelled on release; never throws.
LakesideJourneyWater.ts: lakesideWaterSourceRenderer, prewarmLakesideWaterDraw.
Test: lakeside-journey-water-prewarm (node/mesh/material/slots/size, 2 frames
then removed once, cancel, missing inputs, paused game cap, ordering: show(true)
under black after prime, not from the walk, freed on release).
lakeside-journey-atmosphere show() regex updated for the added call.
